# Who the governance gate actually asks.
#
# The release workflows talk about approval by governance, and until this file
# existed that was a description of an intention rather than a rule anything
# enforced. A required review from a code owner is what turns it into one.
#
# Two things still have to be set in the GitHub UI, because a file in the repo
# cannot grant itself authority:
#
#   Settings > Branches > main: require a pull request, require review from
#   Code Owners, require the `verify` and `browser-specs` checks, and do not
#   allow bypassing. Nothing in CI pushes to `main`, by design, so there is no
#   bot that needs an exemption.
#
#   Settings > Environments > experimental: required reviewers. That is the
#   gate on publishing from a pull request, and it is the one that works for
#   forks, where a workflow gets no secrets and a label proves nothing.
#
# Today this is one person, and naming that plainly is better than a team that
# does not exist yet. Replace with @project-fusion/governance when there is
# someone else in it.

* @irontitan76

